hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1472","On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man’s prayer with everyone is better than his twenty-few prayers alone.” Abu Bakr said: His saying, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A few” is a general word, since a few falls on between three and ten of the number. And he, peace be upon him, explained in the report of Ibn Masoud that she has twenty-five surplus, and he did not say: She does not have except twenty-five, and I know in the report Ibn Umar said that it is superior by twenty-seven degrees."
